==Strategy==
Ultima Beast Naala introduces Multi-Hit Long Distance attacks with multiple effective ranges. Since each hit covers a separate area, Naala is easily stalled, and the main threat of this stage ends up being the Angelic Gories that come out every minute or so. That being said, you should bring a good amount of [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel units]] to minimize its difficulty. Be careful if you use [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], however, as Naala's attacks can heavily damage him regardless of whether or not you have his Resist Curse [[Talents|Talent]].

Since Naala is also a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy, you could potentially use [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|units with the Behemoth Slayer ability]], as curse does not disable it. Likewise, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] can deliver a freeze effect, buying your attackers more time to defeat it as long as Doron's initial attack hits, since Naala is immune to [[Surge Attack|Surges]].

